342 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 177 0 R
/T (1.2. Problem Statement)
/E (1.2. Problem Statement)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 177 0 R
/E (Identifying novel plastic-degrading enzymes from vast microbial genomes remains a significant challenge due to the limitations of current computational models. Existing predictive methods frequently suffer from artificially inflated performance metrics caused by sequence redundancy and train-test data leakage, while simultaneously exhibiting high false-positive rates when attempting to distinguish true polyester-degrading enzymes from structurally similar, non-degrading general hydrolases. Consequently, there is a critical need for a rigorous, homology-aware machine learning framework capable of accurately isolating genuine plastic degradation potential from general enzymatic activity, ensuring reliable discovery through strict dataset curation and hard-negative stress testing.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
