/T (4.2. Risk Identification)
/E (4.2. Risk Identification)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
607 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1504 0 R
/E (Homology-Driven Data Leakage: A primary risk is the potential for sequence similarity between the training and testing datasets to artificially inflate performance metrics. The project mitigates this by using MMseqs2 for homology-aware clustering, ensuring that entire protein families are kept within a single split rather than being shared across boundaries.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
608 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1505 0 R
/E (False Positives from Functional Similarity: There is a technical risk that the model might misclassify general hydrolases \(specifically EC 3.1.1 and 3.1.2\) as plastic-degraders due to their structural similarities. To address this, the system includes a Phase-4 hard negative stress test to verify the model's specificity.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
609 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1506 0 R
/E ("Silver" Tier Data Reliability: Expanding the dataset with homology-propagated "Silver" sequences introduces the risk of including biological noise. This is managed by applying a lower training weight of 0.5 to Silver sequences, compared to the 1.0 weight assigned to "Gold" \(PAZy-curated\) sequences.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
610 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1507 0 R
/E (Metric Saturation on Easy Negatives: The use of broad Swiss-Prot negatives creates a risk of over-optimistic results, such as the near-perfect 1.0 ROC-AUC scores observed. These metrics primarily prove that ESM-2 embeddings can separate basic distributions rather than demonstrating real-world deployment readiness.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
611 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1508 0 R
/E (Threshold-Induced Recall Loss: To maintain high precision and zero false positives on hard negatives, the model operates at a very high probability threshold \(approx. 0.88 for Random Forest\). This presents the risk of a conservative recall rate, where the system identifies only about 52.8% of actual positives.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
612 0 obj
<<
