693 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 1539 0 R
/T (BLAST-Based Expansion \(The "Silver" Tier\): To increase the model's coverage, the Gold sequences were used as queries to search external biological libraries \(such as PlasticDB\) using local BLAST+. To ensure quality, the implementation enforced strict algorithmic filters: only hits meeting a minimum of 90% sequence identity and 90% query coverage were retained. This expanded the pool to 325 raw sequences.)
/E (BLAST-Based Expansion \(The "Silver" Tier\): To increase the model's coverage, the Gold sequences were used as queries to search external biological libraries \(such as PlasticDB\) using local BLAST+. To ensure quality, the implementation enforced strict algorithmic filters: only hits meeting a minimum of 90% sequence identity and 90% query coverage were retained. This expanded the pool to 325 raw sequences.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
694 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 1540 0 R
/T (Integration and Sequence-Level Deduplication: A critical preparation step was the merging of these datasets. Because identical amino acid sequences will yield mathematically identical ESM-2 embeddings, retaining duplicate accessions would artificially inflate the dataset size without adding predictive value. The implementation applied strict sequence-level deduplication, collapsing the raw hits down to 189 canonical, unique positive sequences for training.)
/E (Integration and Sequence-Level Deduplication: A critical preparation step was the merging of these datasets. Because identical amino acid sequences will yield mathematically identical ESM-2 embeddings, retaining duplicate accessions would artificially inflate the dataset size without adding predictive value. The implementation applied strict sequence-level deduplication, collapsing the raw hits down to 189 canonical, unique positive sequences for training.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [3]
>>
