854 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 206 0 R
/E (The rapid accumulation of synthetic plastics in global ecosystems demands scalable and innovative bioremediation solutions. The "PlasticDeg" project successfully addresses a critical bottleneck in this domain by establishing a highly rigorous, computationally honest baseline for discovering novel microbial plastic-degrading enzymes.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
855 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 206 0 R
/E (By prioritizing data integrity above artificially inflated metrics, the developed pipeline effectively mitigates the common pitfalls of bioinformatics machine learning. The implementation of an MMseqs2-driven homology split successfully eradicated train-test data leakage, while the integration of sequence-level deduplication ensured the model learned from unique biological information rather than redundant accessions. Furthermore, the application of a tier-weighted training strategy effectively balanced highly curated "Gold" PAZy data against homology-propagated "Silver" sequences, yielding a highly precise Random Forest classifier.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
856 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 206 0 R
/E (The evaluation results unequivocally demonstrate the representational power of the ESM-2 \(650M\) transformer model. By mapping sequences into a 1280-dimensional latent space, the model achieved perfect precision \(1.0\) and a zero false-positive rate against general Swiss-Prot negatives at its frozen operating threshold. Crucially, the system passed the Phase-4 hard negative stress test, proving that it does not blindly flag generic EC 3.1.1/3.1.2 hydrolases as polyester-degrading enzymes. Ultimately, PlasticDeg proves that deep transfer learning, when bounded by strict biological evaluation frameworks, is a highly reliable tool for triaging vast microbial genomes and isolating genuine plastic-degrading candidates.)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
857 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 206 0 R
/T (9.2 Future Work)
/E (9.2 Future Work)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
858 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 206 0 R
/E (While the PlasticDeg baseline achieves exceptional out-of-sample separability, the intersection of AI and structural biology provides several avenues for future enhancement:)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
