/P 1581 0 R
/T (Enhancing Biological Interpretability \(XAI\): The "black box" nature of deep transformer embeddings limits biochemical interpretability. Future work should focus on Explainable AI \(XAI\) techniques, such as applying attention-mapping algorithms to the transformer heads. This would allow researchers to trace the model's predictions back to specific amino acid residues, potentially highlighting novel catalytic triads or mutational hotspots for directed evolution.)
/E (Enhancing Biological Interpretability \(XAI\): The "black box" nature of deep transformer embeddings limits biochemical interpretability. Future work should focus on Explainable AI \(XAI\) techniques, such as applying attention-mapping algorithms to the transformer heads. This would allow researchers to trace the model's predictions back to specific amino acid residues, potentially highlighting novel catalytic triads or mutational hotspots for directed evolution.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
865 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 1582 0 R
/T (Continuous Metagenomic Pipeline Expansion: As the plastisphere expands, newly sequenced microbial genomes are constantly deposited into public databases. The current architecture's incremental .npz caching system is designed to scale. Future updates should automate the ingestion of broader metagenomic datasets, utilizing the current frozen model in a semi-supervised learning loop to continuously mine for rare degradation pathways.)
/E (Continuous Metagenomic Pipeline Expansion: As the plastisphere expands, newly sequenced microbial genomes are constantly deposited into public databases. The current architecture's incremental .npz caching system is designed to scale. Future updates should automate the ingestion of broader metagenomic datasets, utilizing the current frozen model in a semi-supervised learning loop to continuously mine for rare degradation pathways.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
