2605 0 obj
<<
/Title (7.5.1 Embedding Separability and Threshold Dynamics The near-perfect classification metrics observed on the easy test negatives are an honest reflection of the representational power of the ESM-2 embeddings. The 1280-dimensional vectors effectively map the complex structural and evolutionary signatures of the sequences, creating a highly distinct mathematical boundary between true plastic-degrading enzymes and general protein backgrounds. An analysis of the prediction confidence distributions illustrates this sharp clustering. True negative sequences are overwhelmingly scored near zero, while true positives push heavily toward a probability of one. This strict separation justifies the methodological decision to dynamically freeze the operating threshold at a highly restrictive 0.879 \(to target an 80% training recall\) rather than defaulting to a standard 0.5 cutoff.)
/Dest [42 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2599 0 R
/Next 2606 0 R
>>
endobj
2606 0 obj
<<
/Title (Page | 34                                   DEPARTMENT OF INFORMATION SCIENCE & ENGINEERING)
