/Title (A deeper breakdown of the classifier's performance is required to fully understand its behavior across the imbalanced dataset. Because microbial plastic degradation is a rare enzymatic trait compared to general metabolic functions, the model must avoid over-predicting positives. The per-class evaluation metrics confirm that the Random Forest model is inherently conservative at the frozen threshold. It achieves a perfect precision score for the positive class, ensuring that any sequence it flags as a plastic-degrading enzyme is highly reliable and free from background Swiss-Prot noise. However, this strictness naturally limits the recall, indicating that the model prioritizes absolute diagnostic certainty over broad, unverified discovery.)
/Dest [41 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 2620 0 R
/Next 2604 0 R
>>
endobj
