2615 0 obj
<<
/Title (7.5.2 Interpretability Challenges and Model Limitations Despite the strong predictive capabilities and the successful Phase-4 stress test against hard negatives, the framework exhibits inherent limitations typical of deep transfer-learning architectures. Specifically, the system faces a severe biological interpretability challenge. While ensemble models like Random Forest inherently calculate and rank feature importance to explain their decision-making process, the input features in this pipeline are highly abstract. Because the inputs are 1280-dimensional latent tensors extracted from the 33rd layer of a transformer model, the "most important" numerical features driving the classification cannot be easily reverse-engineered into physical biochemistry.)
/Dest [43 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2606 0 R
/Prev 2614 0 R
>>
endobj
